N = {
"Genesis": [
"God creates the heavens and the earth in six days, makes people in his own image, and rests on the seventh. He calls everything he made good.",
"God finishes creation and rests on the seventh day. He forms Adam from the dust and makes Eve from Adam's side, and the two become one.",
"The serpent tempts Eve, and she and Adam eat the forbidden fruit. Sin enters the world. God promises that a child of the woman will one day crush the serpent.",
"Cain and Abel bring offerings. God accepts Abel's and not Cain's, and in anger Cain kills his brother. God marks Cain and sends him away.",
"This is the family line from Adam to Noah, ten generations. It records that people lived very long lives, and that Enoch walked with God and was taken.",
"People grow wicked and violent, and God grieves. But Noah finds favor with God. God tells him to build an ark and gives him its measurements.",
"The flood comes. Noah, his family and the animals go into the ark, and the waters cover the earth for forty days of rain.",
"The waters go down and the ark comes to rest on the mountains of Ararat. Noah sends out a raven and a dove. He leaves the ark and offers a sacrifice.",
"God blesses Noah and sets the rainbow in the sky as his promise never to flood the whole earth again. Noah's sons spread out to fill the land.",
"This chapter lists the nations that came from Noah's three sons, Shem, Ham and Japheth. It shows how the peoples of the world are all related.",
"People build a tower at Babel to make a name for themselves. God confuses their language and scatters them. The chapter then names Abram's family line.",
"God calls Abram to leave his home and promises to make him a great nation and bless all peoples through him. Abram obeys and travels to Canaan.",
"Abram and his nephew Lot have too many animals to share the land, so they part ways. Lot chooses the rich Jordan valley. God repeats his promise of land to Abram.",
"Four kings capture Lot in a war. Abram rescues him. The priest-king Melchizedek brings out bread and wine and blesses Abram.",
"God promises Abram as many descendants as the stars. Abram believes, and God counts it to him as righteousness. God makes a covenant with him.",
"Sarai gives her servant Hagar to Abram, and Hagar bears Ishmael. Sarai treats her harshly and Hagar flees. An angel finds her and promises that her son will have many descendants.",
"God renames Abram Abraham and Sarai Sarah. He makes circumcision the sign of his covenant and promises that Sarah will have a son named Isaac.",
"Three visitors come to Abraham's tent, and he welcomes them. They promise Sarah a son. Abraham pleads with God to spare Sodom if righteous people are found there.",
"Two angels reach Sodom, and the men of the city turn violent. The angels lead Lot and his daughters out. God destroys Sodom and Gomorrah, and Lot's wife looks back and becomes a pillar of salt.",
"Abraham again says that Sarah is his sister, and King Abimelech takes her. God warns the king in a dream, and he gives her back.",
"Isaac is born to Abraham and Sarah when they are old, just as God promised. Sarah sends Hagar and Ishmael away. God cares for them in the wilderness.",
"God tests Abraham by telling him to offer Isaac as a sacrifice. At the last moment an angel stops him, and God provides a ram instead. God repeats his promises.",
"Sarah dies at age 127. Abraham buys a field and cave at Machpelah from the Hittites and buries her there. It is his first piece of land in Canaan.",
"Abraham sends his servant to find a wife for Isaac. At a well the servant meets Rebekah, who gives him water and agrees to go. She marries Isaac.",
"Abraham dies and is buried beside Sarah. The chapter lists Ishmael's sons, then tells of the birth of the twins Esau and Jacob. Esau sells his birthright for a bowl of stew.",
"A famine comes and Isaac stays in Gerar. He digs wells and the Philistines argue with him over them. God renews to Isaac the promise made to Abraham.",
"Isaac, old and blind, plans to bless Esau. Rebekah helps Jacob disguise himself, and Jacob receives the blessing instead. Esau is furious and wants to kill him.",
"Isaac sends Jacob to Laban's house to find a wife. On the way Jacob dreams of a ladder to heaven, and God promises him the land and descendants. Jacob names the place Bethel.",
"Jacob reaches Haran and meets Rachel at a well. He works seven years to marry her, but Laban tricks him into marrying her sister Leah first. Leah bears Jacob's first sons.",
"Rachel is unable to have children, and Leah's servants and Rachel's servants also bear sons to Jacob. Finally Rachel gives birth to Joseph.",
"Jacob and Laban argue over wages and Jacob's flocks grow large. Jacob takes his family and flees. Laban chases him, and they make a covenant at Galeed.",
"Jacob sends gifts ahead and prepares to meet Esau. That night he wrestles with a man until dawn and is renamed Israel, because he has struggled with God and people and prevailed.",
"Jacob sees Esau coming with four hundred men and bows to the ground seven times. Esau runs to meet him and embraces him, and the brothers are reconciled. Jacob settles near Shechem.",
"Dinah, Jacob's daughter, is seized by a man of Shechem. Her brothers Simeon and Levi kill the men of the city in revenge. Jacob is troubled by what they did.",
"God sends Jacob back to Bethel, and Jacob has his household put away their idols. Rachel dies giving birth to Benjamin. Isaac dies and Jacob and Esau bury him.",
"This chapter lists Esau's descendants, the Edomites, and the kings and chiefs who came from him.",
"Jacob loves Joseph most and gives him a long coat. Joseph tells his brothers his dreams, and they hate him. They sell him to traders heading for Egypt and tell Jacob he is dead.",
"Judah marries and has sons. After his sons die, Tamar disguises herself to get a child from Judah, and she bears twins, Perez and Zerah. Perez is an ancestor of Jesus.",
"Joseph serves in Potiphar's house in Egypt and does well. Potiphar's wife falsely accuses him, and Joseph is thrown into prison. God is with him there.",
"In prison Joseph correctly explains the dreams of the king's cupbearer and baker. The cupbearer is restored to his job, but he forgets Joseph.",
"Pharaoh has two troubling dreams. The cupbearer remembers Joseph, who explains that seven good years will be followed by seven years of famine. Pharaoh makes Joseph his chief official.",
"Famine strikes. Jacob sends ten of his sons to buy grain in Egypt, and Joseph recognizes them but they do not know him. He holds Simeon until they bring back Benjamin.",
"The famine continues, and Jacob lets Benjamin go with his brothers. Joseph welcomes them to a meal and then has his silver cup hidden in Benjamin's sack.",
"The cup is found in Benjamin's sack. Judah offers himself as a slave in Benjamin's place, so that their father will not be heartbroken.",
"Joseph can no longer hold back and tells his brothers who he is. He tells them God sent him ahead to save lives. He invites his whole family to Egypt.",
"Jacob learns that Joseph is alive and sets out for Egypt. God speaks to him at Beersheba and promises to go with him. Jacob's family of seventy settles in Egypt.",
"Joseph presents his father and brothers to Pharaoh, who gives them the land of Goshen. Jacob blesses Pharaoh. The famine grows worse, and Joseph buys the land and people for Pharaoh in exchange for grain.",
"Jacob, near death, asks Joseph to promise to bury him in Canaan. Joseph brings his sons Ephraim and Manasseh, and Jacob blesses them, putting the younger Ephraim first.",
"Jacob gives a blessing to each of his twelve sons. Judah is promised that the ruler's scepter will come from his line. Jacob dies and asks to be buried with his fathers.",
"Joseph mourns for Jacob and the Egyptians mourn for seventy days. The family buries him in Canaan. Joseph forgives his brothers, saying God meant their harm for good. He dies in Egypt and asks that his bones be carried home."
],
"Exodus": [
"The Israelites grow numerous in Egypt, and a new Pharaoh enslaves them. He orders the Hebrew baby boys thrown in the river. The midwives refuse.",
"Moses is born and hidden in a basket on the Nile. Pharaoh's daughter finds him and raises him. As a man he kills an Egyptian, flees to Midian and marries Zipporah.",
"God speaks to Moses from a burning bush and sends him to free the Israelites. God gives his name, I AM, and promises to be with Moses.",
"Moses worries that he cannot speak well. God gives him signs to show and sends his brother Aaron to speak for him. Moses returns to Egypt.",
"Moses and Aaron ask Pharaoh to let the people go to worship. Pharaoh refuses and makes the Israelites' work harder. The people blame Moses.",
"God promises again to rescue Israel and to be their God. The chapter lists the family lines of Moses and Aaron.",
"God tells Moses and Aaron to go to Pharaoh. Aaron's staff becomes a snake and swallows the Egyptian magicians' snakes. The Nile is turned to blood.",
"Frogs cover Egypt, and then gnats and then flies. Pharaoh says he will let the people go, but he changes his mind each time.",
"God sends a plague on the livestock, then boils, then hail. Pharaoh admits his sin but hardens his heart again.",
"Locusts eat what the hail left, and then three days of thick darkness cover Egypt. Pharaoh still will not let Israel go.",
"God tells Moses that one more plague will come, the death of every firstborn in Egypt. The Israelites ask their neighbors for silver and gold.",
"God sets up the first Passover. Each family kills a lamb and puts its blood on the doorposts, so that the destroyer will pass over their houses. At midnight the firstborn of Egypt die, and Pharaoh sends the Israelites out.",
"God tells Israel to set apart every firstborn to him and to remember the Exodus. A pillar of cloud by day and a pillar of fire by night lead them.",
"Pharaoh chases the Israelites to the Red Sea. God parts the sea and Israel crosses on dry ground. The water returns and drowns the Egyptian army.",
"Moses and Miriam lead the people in a song of praise to God. Then the people find only bitter water at Marah. God makes it sweet.",
"The people complain of hunger in the desert. God sends quail in the evening and manna each morning, and gives rules for gathering it and keeping the Sabbath.",
"The people have no water and test God at Massah and Meribah. Moses strikes the rock and water flows. Israel then fights Amalek, and wins while Moses holds up his hands.",
"Moses' father-in-law Jethro visits and sees Moses worn out by judging the people. He advises Moses to appoint other capable men as judges.",
"Israel camps at Mount Sinai. God offers to make them his treasured people, a kingdom of priests. The people agree, and God prepares to speak to them.",
"God gives the Ten Commandments: no other gods, no idols, respect God's name, keep the Sabbath, honor your parents, and do not murder, commit adultery, steal, lie or covet.",
"God gives laws about altars, slaves, violence, and injuries. The laws protect the weak and set fair penalties.",
"God gives laws about property, borrowing, and promises. Some laws protect widows and orphans, and some forbid charging the poor interest.",
"God gives laws about justice, the Sabbath year and the three yearly feasts. He promises to send an angel before Israel into the land.",
"Israel agrees to keep the covenant, and Moses seals it with blood. Moses goes up the mountain for forty days and nights with God.",
"God tells Moses to collect offerings for building a sanctuary. He describes the ark of the covenant, the table and the lampstand.",
"God describes the tent of meeting, its curtains and its frames. The tent is the place where God will live among his people.",
"God describes the altar for burnt offerings and the courtyard around the tent.",
"God describes the clothes for the priests, including the breastplate with twelve stones for the twelve tribes.",
"God sets out how Aaron and his sons are to be made priests. They are washed, dressed, anointed and offer sacrifices. God promises to live among Israel.",
"God describes the altar of incense, the bronze basin and the holy anointing oil. He also tells Moses to count the people, and each man pays a half shekel.",
"God names Bezalel and Oholiab as skilled craftsmen filled with his Spirit. He tells Moses again to keep the Sabbath, and gives him two stone tablets.",
"Moses is slow to come down the mountain, so the people ask Aaron for a god. He makes a golden calf. Moses breaks the tablets and the people are punished.",
"Moses pleads for the people and God agrees to go with them. Moses asks to see God's glory, and God lets him see his back as he passes.",
"God makes new tablets and renews the covenant. He proclaims himself merciful, gracious and slow to anger. Moses' face shines.",
"Moses gathers Israel and passes on the Sabbath law. The people bring more gifts than are needed for the tent.",
"The craftsmen build the tent. They weave the curtains and make the frames, the bars and the veil, just as God told Moses.",
"Bezalel makes the ark of the covenant, the table for the bread, the lampstand and the altar of incense.",
"Bezalel makes the altar for burnt offerings, the bronze basin and the courtyard. The chapter lists the gold, silver and bronze used.",
"The craftsmen make the priests' clothes, including the breastplate with twelve stones. Moses inspects all the work and blesses the people.",
"Moses sets up the tent on the first day of the new year and puts everything in place. A cloud covers the tent and the glory of the Lord fills it. The cloud shows Israel when to move and when to stay."
],
"Leviticus": [
"God tells Moses how to offer the burnt offering. A person brings an animal without blemish, and the priest offers it on the altar.",
"God describes the grain offering, made of flour, oil and incense. Honey and yeast are not allowed, but salt is required.",
"God describes the peace offering, a shared meal. The fat belongs to God, and the people may not eat fat or blood.",
"God describes the sin offering for sins done by mistake. The offering differs depending on whether the sinner is a priest, the whole people, a leader or an ordinary person.",
"God describes the guilt offering and how to make amends for sins such as keeping silent when asked to testify or touching something unclean. Poor people may bring birds or flour.",
"Anyone who steals, cheats or lies must pay back in full plus one fifth and then bring a guilt offering. God gives rules for the daily fire on the altar.",
"God gives more rules for the offerings and says which portions the priests may eat. He forbids eating fat and blood.",
"Moses washes and dresses Aaron and his sons and anoints them as priests. They offer sacrifices for seven days.",
"On the eighth day Aaron offers the first sacrifices for the people. Fire comes from the Lord and burns the offering, and the people shout and bow down.",
"Aaron's sons Nadab and Abihu offer unauthorized fire and die. Moses tells Aaron that God must be treated as holy. God warns priests not to drink wine when serving.",
"God tells Israel which animals they may eat and which they may not. He says: be holy, for I am holy.",
"After giving birth, a woman is unclean for a set time. When it ends she brings an offering to the priest. A boy is circumcised on the eighth day.",
"God gives rules for skin diseases. The priest examines the person, and those found unclean must live outside the camp until they are healed.",
"A person who has been healed of a skin disease goes through a ritual to be made clean. God also gives rules for mold in houses.",
"God gives rules about bodily discharges, which make a person unclean for a time. The person washes and waits to become clean again.",
"On the Day of Atonement the high priest enters the Most Holy Place and offers sacrifices for himself and the people. A goat is sent into the wilderness carrying the people's sins.",
"God forbids sacrificing anywhere but the tent of meeting. He forbids eating blood, because the life is in the blood.",
"God forbids Israel to copy the practices of Egypt and Canaan. He gives rules about forbidden marriages and sexual relations.",
"God says: be holy. He gives commands about honoring parents, caring for the poor, being honest and fair, and loving your neighbor as yourself.",
"God sets penalties for worshipping Molech, for cursing parents, and for serious sexual sins. He says Israel is to be set apart from the other nations.",
"God gives special rules for priests. They must not make themselves unclean by touching the dead, and they must marry only women who are fit for the priesthood.",
"God says that sacrificial animals must be without defect. He tells priests to treat the offerings with respect.",
"God lists the feasts: the Sabbath, Passover, Unleavened Bread, Firstfruits, Weeks, Trumpets, the Day of Atonement and Booths.",
"God tells Moses to keep the lamps burning and to set out twelve loaves of bread in the tent. A man curses God's name and is stoned to death.",
"Every seventh year the land rests. Every fiftieth year is the Jubilee, when land returns to its family and slaves go free. God promises to provide for those who obey.",
"God promises blessings if Israel keeps his covenant: good harvests, peace and his presence. He warns of curses if they refuse. He promises to remember the covenant even if they are scattered.",
"God gives rules for vows and for paying the value of persons and property promised to him. He says that the tenth of the harvest and of the flocks belongs to him."
]
}
